(Note: This file exists mainly for copyright purposes rather than
 credit-giving, so tries to describe only who wrote what files rather
 than who provided e.g. important-but-short bug-fixes.)

Stephen Tweedie: Main author of the defrag package.

Alexey Vovenko and Ulrich Habel: Adaptation for the xia, ext2
filesystem and the picture option.

Linus Torvalds and Remy Card: Authors of the fsck and e2fsck programs,
which served as a basis for the initial version.

Theodore Ts'o: llseek.c, llseek parts of configure.in.

Peter Moulder: configure.in (other than llseek stuff).  tests/*.
Changes specific to ext2 features sparse_super, compression.

The current maintainer is Phillip Susi <psusi@ubuntu.com>
